    "title": "AI agent account impairing a security or autonomous defense",
    "desc": "An AI agent account stopped, disabled, killed or rewrote the config of a security / EDR / defense tool - banken or mimi itself, CrowdStrike Falcon, osquery, Wazuh, auditd, Laurel, ClamAV, Microsoft Defender (mdatp), Suricata, Zeek, OSSEC, AIDE, Tripwire. This is the host-observable form of MITRE T1685.007 Impair Autonomous Defenses (new in ATT&CK v20): the technique's framing is an attacker using (indirect) prompt injection to get an AI-driven system to ignore or disable its own defensive capability. banken cannot read the injected prompt, but it sees the agent account taking down the defensive tooling - the realised effect, and a clean signal because an agent account has no business stopping the host's EDR. tamper_banken and the disable_* rules catch this host-wide; this is the account-scoped, autonomous-defense framing for the agentic-detection set.\nThis is an \"agentic AI detection\" rule. See rules/agent/README.md. (ATT&CK v20 places T1685 under the new Defense Impairment tactic; banken keeps the attack.defense-evasion tag until the Navigator-layer v20 bump remaps tactic strings tree-wide.)",
